 "text": "Hey, good to have you back. How are you? Bicycle fitting is making bike fit the person, rather than the other way around. It starts with your body position on the bike, and then extends to other aspects of the bike. He's bit of a showman. The real test is how you feel. A properly fitted bike means you shouldn't be in pain after an hour. Then you probably need a shorter stem and some padding under the bar tape. Not necessarily. A short stem and some bar tape are cheap. A quick check is fine. A proper fit takes about half an hour and are worth it if it means ending your Saturday afternoons on the sofa.",
